# core.autocrlf is on in this clone, which makes git announce a CRLF rewrite for
# every file it touches and hands shell scripts a carriage return that `sh` chokes
# on. These paths are the fork's own (see docs/guide/fork-workflow-for-agents.md)
# and are all stored with LF already, so pinning them changes no content - it only
# keeps the working copy correct and the output quiet.
#
# Deliberately NOT a blanket `* text=auto`: that would renormalise upstream's files
# and turn the hourly sync into a tree-wide conflict.
.gitattributes      text eol=lf
.githooks/**        text eol=lf
.claude/**          text eol=lf
scripts/dev/**      text eol=lf
docs/guide/**       text eol=lf
reverse-toolkit/**  text eol=lf
